# ─── Elecbits ULM portal — environment ──────────────────────────────────────
# Same Supabase project as the ODM PMS app — the ULM portal reads the same
# core.* spine (people, orgs, projects) and writes through the ulm.* schema.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Every integration degrades gracefully when unset.

# ── Supabase (shared with the ODM PMS) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Project → Settings → API. Run supabase/10-ulm-tool.sql first, and add `ulm`
# (alongside `core` and `pms`) to Settings → API → Exposed schemas.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon public key>

# ── Google Drive provisioning (google-apps-script/ulm-drive.gs) ─────────────
# The deployed Apps Script web app that owns the Client-ID / Project-ID
# register sheets, replicates the project template folder and links the
# eb-templates library into the process-map sheet. Empty → the portal still
# works: IDs generate locally and Drive steps show as pending seams.
# VITE_ULM_DRIVE_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/<deployment-id>/exec
# VITE_ULM_DRIVE_TOKEN=<must match SHARED_TOKEN in ulm-drive.gs>

# ── Anthropic (AI-drafted LLDs) — optional ──────────────────────────────────
# Point at the same `claude` Edge Function the ODM app uses. Empty → the LLD
# gates fall back to structured manual entry.
# VITE_CLAUDE_PROXY_URL=https://<project-ref>.functions.supabase.co/claude
